# EAS archive rules. NOTE: when .easignore exists, eas-cli IGNORES every
# .gitignore (root + nested) for archiving — this file must therefore carry
# all of their rules itself. It exists for exactly one deviation:
#   packages/react-native-engine-native/ios/EngineNative.xcframework
#   packages/react-native-secp-native/ios/SecpNative.xcframework
# are gitignored build artifacts that MUST be in the EAS build archive
# (EngineNative.podspec / SecpNative.podspec vendor them; pod install fails
# without them). Build + sync them before an EAS build:
#   (cd native-engine-ffi && scripts/build-engine-xcframework.sh)
#   (cd native-secp-poc  && scripts/build-secp-xcframework.sh)
#   packages/react-native-engine-native/scripts/sync-xcframework.sh
#   packages/react-native-secp-native/scripts/sync-xcframework.sh

# --- from .gitignore (root) ---
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
/.windsurfrules

.env

*.apk
*.ipa
android
# Workspace packages ship their own tracked Android native module sources
# (Nitro modules autolinked on Android) under packages/*/android — keep those
# out of the bare `android` rule above, which exists to ignore the top-level
# Expo-generated /android app dir and any incidental `android` directories
# elsewhere (e.g. credentials/android, which must stay ignored).
#
# This mirrors .gitignore's own negation for the same reason — but it is a
# SEPARATE file that duplicates the rule, not an inherited one: eas-cli
# ignores every .gitignore outright once .easignore exists (see the header
# above), so a negation added to .gitignore later never reaches here on its
# own. This exact gap silently stripped packages/react-native-localpay-
# transport/android/ out of every EAS-built archive from the day that Nitro
# module was scaffolded (2026-07-29) until this fix (2026-07-31) — the
# module was never merely unregistered on device, it was never IN the build
# at all. Found only because a from-source `nm` check of the shipped .so
# would have been the next diagnostic step; check the EAS build log's own
# file listing (not just "gradle succeeded") whenever a native module that
# lives under packages/*/android stops showing up in a build's task list.
#
# `**` (any depth), not `*` (one level): a single-level negation still lets
# the bare `android` rule above strip nitrogen's OWN generated glue at
# packages/react-native-localpay-transport/nitrogen/generated/android/ (a
# sibling of the package's ios/android/shared dirs, not a child of it) —
# confirmed the hard way: `git ls-files --exclude-from .easignore --ignored
# --cached` still listed all ten files under nitrogen/generated/android/
# after the first (single-level) version of this fix, and the next EAS
# build failed at Gradle configuration ("Could not read script
# .../LocalPayTransport+autolinking.gradle as it does not exist") rather
# than silently omitting the module the way the missing top-level android/
# had. Re-run that exact `git ls-files` command against this file after any
# future edit here — it is the fast, no-build way to prove what an EAS
# archive will actually contain.
!/packages/**/android
!/packages/**/android/**

# ...but still ignore Gradle/CMake build output nested inside tracked
# package android/ dirs (single-level: nitrogen's generated/android/ has no
# build/.cxx of its own, only the package's own top-level android/ does).
packages/*/android/build
packages/*/android/.cxx

expo-env.d.ts
.expo
*.aab
/BSVBrowser.app
build-*.tar.gz
/@bsvb__bsv-browser.jks
docs/marketing
marketing.html
Dev Builds.zip
.opencode
credentials.json
.superpowers/

# --- from ios/.gitignore (path-prefixed) ---
ios/build/
*.pbxuser
!default.pbxuser
*.mode1v3
!default.mode1v3
*.mode2v3
!default.mode2v3
*.perspectivev3
!default.perspectivev3
xcuserdata
*.xccheckout
*.moved-aside
DerivedData
*.hmap
*.xcuserstate
project.xcworkspace
.xcode.env.local
*.jsbundle
ios/Pods/

# --- Rust build dirs (nested .gitignores) ---
native-engine-ffi/target/
native-engine-poc/target/
native-secp-poc/target/
native-secp-poc/sdk-2.1.6/

# FFI source-package xcframeworks stay OUT of the archive — the pods consume
# the pre-synced copies under packages/react-native-*-native/ios/, which are
# deliberately NOT listed here (the whole point of this file).
native-engine-ffi/packages/EngineNativeFFI/EngineNative.xcframework/
native-secp-poc/packages/SecpNativeFFI/SecpNative.xcframework/
